      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Scope \u0026 Commit Message Structure**\n\n1. **Single Logical Change (Split into Two Stacked CLs):** The subject line joins two distinct actions with `\" and \"` (`Keep FSCE# asserted` and `delay during flash status polling`), and the patch bundles two independently committable changes that can each build and be verified on their own:\n   - **CL 1:** Keep `FSCE#` asserted across flash status polling in `dma_flash_cmd_read_status()` by issuing `FLASH_CMD_RS` once, reading status directly from `IT83XX_SMFI_ECINDDR`, and driving `FSCE#` high only after the expected status is observed.\n   - **CL 2:** Add the ~15 us `IT83XX_GCTRL_WNCKR` delay inside the `dma_flash_cmd_read_status()` polling loop to throttle `IT83XX_SMFI_ECINDDR` reads (matching `crrev.com/c/8119380`).\n\n2. **Explain *Why* (Problem Impact) Rather Than Narrating the Code:**\n   - The first paragraph describes *what* the old code did mechanically (`\"repeatedly toggles FSCE# and resends FLASH_CMD_RS in a tight loop with no delay\"`), and the second paragraph narrates the replacement statements step-by-step (`\"Send FLASH_CMD_RS once while keeping FSCE# asserted, delay via IT83XX_GCTRL_WNCKR (~15 us)...\"`).\n   - Instead, state **why** the previous behavior was problematic (repeatedly toggling `FSCE#` and re-sending `FLASH_CMD_RS` adds unnecessary SPI transaction overhead on every status check, and unthrottled back-to-back reads of `IT83XX_SMFI_ECINDDR` while flash is busy can cause bus contention or premature status evaluation resulting in intermittent flash erase/write failures) and summarize the fix at a conceptual level.\n\n### Suggested Commit Messages (When Split into Two CLs)\n\n**CL 1:**\n```text\nchip/it83xx: Keep FSCE# asserted during flash status polling\n\ndma_flash_cmd_read_status() previously executed a full transaction on\nevery poll iteration, toggling FSCE# and resending FLASH_CMD_RS for\neach status byte read. Because SPI flash shifts out the latest status\nregister value continuously while FSCE# remains low after FLASH_CMD_RS,\nre-issuing the command on every poll adds unnecessary transaction\noverhead while waiting for flash operations to complete.\n\nKeep FSCE# asserted after sending FLASH_CMD_RS once, poll the status\nregister until the target mask matches, and deassert FSCE# when polling\ncompletes.\n\nBUG\u003db:574033256\nTEST\u003dmake run-flash_it83xx\nTEST\u003dmake BOARD\u003dasurada -j; verify flash write/erase status polling\n```\n\n**CL 2:**\n```text\nchip/it83xx: Delay between flash status register reads\n\nPolling IT83XX_SMFI_ECINDDR in a tight loop with no delay while flash is\nbusy can cause bus contention or premature status evaluation on fast\nsilicon and higher compiler optimization levels, leading to intermittent\nflash write and erase failures.\n\nInsert a ~15 us hardware delay between status register reads during\npolling, matching Zephyr\u0027s ramcode_flash_cmd_read_status()\n(crrev.com/c/8119380).\n\nBUG\u003db:574033256\nTEST\u003dmake run-flash_it83xx\nTEST\u003dmake BOARD\u003dasurada -j; verify flash write/erase status polling\n```\n\n### Suggested Commit Message (If Kept as a Single CL)\n```text\nchip/it83xx: Throttle continuous flash status polling\n\ndma_flash_cmd_read_status() previously toggled FSCE# and re-issued\nFLASH_CMD_RS in an unthrottled loop on every status check. Re-sending\nthe command on every poll adds unnecessary SPI transaction overhead,\nand back-to-back status reads without a delay can cause bus contention\nor premature status evaluation during flash write and erase operations.\n\nKeep FSCE# asserted across a single FLASH_CMD_RS transaction and delay\n~15 us between status reads until the target status is observed,\nmatching Zephyr\u0027s ramcode_flash_cmd_read_status() (crrev.com/c/8119380).\n\nBUG\u003db:574033256\nTEST\u003dmake run-flash_it83xx\nTEST\u003dmake BOARD\u003dasurada -j; verify flash write/erase status polling\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/637b0f