      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Split Logical Changes \u0026 Add Unit Test Coverage**\n\n### 1. Split into Two Focused Changes\nThis function change combines two independent improvements that should be landed as stacked CLs:\n\n- **CL 1 (Keep `FSCE#` asserted across status polling):**\n```c\nvoid FLASH_DMA_CODE dma_flash_cmd_read_status(enum flash_status_mask mask,\n\t\t\t\t\t      enum flash_status_mask target)\n{\n\tuint8_t cmd_rs[] \u003d { FLASH_CMD_RS };\n\n\t/* Send read status command */\n\tdma_flash_transaction(sizeof(cmd_rs), cmd_rs, 0, NULL, 0);\n\n\t/*\n\t * We prefer no timeout here. We can always get the status\n\t * we want, or wait for watchdog triggered to check\n\t * e-flash\u0027s status before CPU reset.\n\t * This will avoid fetching unknown instruction from e-flash\n\t * and causing exception.\n\t */\n\twhile ((IT83XX_SMFI_ECINDDR \u0026 mask) !\u003d target)\n\t\t;\n\n\t/* Transaction done, drive FSCE# high */\n\tdma_flash_fsce_high();\n}\n```\n\n- **CL 2 (Add the ~15 us `IT83XX_GCTRL_WNCKR` polling delay):**\n```c\n\twhile ((IT83XX_SMFI_ECINDDR \u0026 mask) !\u003d target)\n\t\tIT83XX_GCTRL_WNCKR \u003d 0;\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Add Automated Unit Test Coverage\n`dma_flash_cmd_read_status()` implements transaction framing (`FSCE#` kept low during `FLASH_CMD_RS`, then driven high via `dma_flash_fsce_high()`), bitmask filtering (`(IT83XX_SMFI_ECINDDR \u0026 mask) !\u003d target`), and delay pacing (`IT83XX_GCTRL_WNCKR \u003d 0`), but this CL only lists manual board verification (`TEST\u003dmake BOARD\u003dasurada -j; verify flash write/erase status polling`).\n\nPlease add a host unit test (e.g., `test/flash_it83xx.c`) or a small register-access seam in `chip/it83xx/flash.c` so `dma_flash_cmd_read_status()` is covered by automated tests for:\n1. **Immediate status match on first read:** `(IT83XX_SMFI_ECINDDR \u0026 mask) \u003d\u003d target` on the initial check executes 0 loop delay writes and drives `FSCE#` high.\n2. **Multi-iteration busy-to-ready transition:** Polling while `FLASH_SR_BUSY` is set for $N$ reads before clearing issues `FLASH_CMD_RS` only once (with `stop_ec_ind \u003d 0`), writes `0` to `IT83XX_GCTRL_WNCKR` on each non-matching read, and calls `dma_flash_fsce_high()` once at the end.\n3. **Bitmask isolation:** Unmasked bits in `IT83XX_SMFI_ECINDDR` (such as `FLASH_SR_WEL` when polling `mask \u003d FLASH_SR_BUSY, target \u003d FLASH_SR_NO_BUSY`) are ignored, whereas full-mask checks (`mask \u003d FLASH_SR_ALL, target \u003d FLASH_SR_WEL`) continue polling until both `WEL \u003d\u003d 1` and `BUSY \u003d\u003d 0`.\n\nExample unit test harness (if `IT83XX_SMFI_ECINDDR` / `IT83XX_GCTRL_WNCKR` reads and writes are routed through small inline helpers or overridden in a test build):\n```c\nstruct flash_poll_test_state {\n\tconst uint8_t *status_seq;\n\tsize_t status_len;\n\tsize_t status_idx;\n\tint wnckr_writes;\n\tint fsce_high_calls;\n};\n\nstatic int test_read_status_immediate_match(void)\n{\n\tconst uint8_t seq[] \u003d { FLASH_SR_NO_BUSY };\n\treset_flash_poll_state(seq, ARRAY_SIZE(seq));\n\n\tdma_flash_cmd_read_status(FLASH_SR_BUSY, FLASH_SR_NO_BUSY);\n\n\tTEST_EQ(poll_state.status_idx, 1, \"%zu\");\n\tTEST_EQ(poll_state.wnckr_writes, 0, \"%d\");\n\tTEST_EQ(poll_state.fsce_high_calls, 1, \"%d\");\n\treturn EC_SUCCESS;\n}\n\nstatic int test_read_status_busy_then_ready(void)\n{\n\tconst uint8_t seq[] \u003d {\n\t\tFLASH_SR_BUSY,\n\t\tFLASH_SR_BUSY,\n\t\tFLASH_SR_NO_BUSY,\n\t};\n\treset_flash_poll_state(seq, ARRAY_SIZE(seq));\n\n\tdma_flash_cmd_read_status(FLASH_SR_BUSY, FLASH_SR_NO_BUSY);\n\n\tTEST_EQ(poll_state.status_idx, 3, \"%zu\");\n\tTEST_EQ(poll_state.wnckr_writes, 2, \"%d\");\n\tTEST_EQ(poll_state.fsce_high_calls, 1, \"%d\");\n\treturn EC_SUCCESS;\n}\n\nstatic int test_read_status_mask_filtering(void)\n{\n\t/* WEL bit set while checking only BUSY mask should match immediately; */\n\t/* checking FLASH_SR_ALL for FLASH_SR_WEL should wait for BUSY to clear. */\n\tconst uint8_t seq[] \u003d {\n\t\tFLASH_SR_WEL | FLASH_SR_BUSY,\n\t\tFLASH_SR_WEL,\n\t};\n\treset_flash_poll_state(seq, ARRAY_SIZE(seq));\n\n\tdma_flash_cmd_read_status(FLASH_SR_ALL, FLASH_SR_WEL);\n\n\tTEST_EQ(poll_state.status_idx, 2, \"%zu\");\n\tTEST_EQ(poll_state.wnckr_writes, 1, \"%d\");\n\tTEST_EQ(poll_state.fsce_high_calls, 1, \"%d\");\n\treturn EC_SUCCESS;\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/637b0f37-10bc-49de-bcb0-c9bbabdc1f09)",
